Claude Integration

This folder contains Claude-related configuration and development files for the Valley of AI project.

settings.local.json

Local development configuration file that documents the Claude-assisted development workflow for this project.

How Claude Was Used

Claude was integrated into the development process at multiple stages:

Local Development Setup — Claude helped configure local servers and development environments
Problem-Solving — Used Claude for debugging, architecture decisions, and optimization
Research & Data Collection — Claude assisted in researching Bay Area AI installations and organizing data
Content Generation — Claude helped write descriptions and analyze AI trends
Code Development — Claude provided code suggestions and architectural guidance
Key Development Commands

The settings.local.json file includes bash commands for:

Python HTTP Server — Local testing environment for gallery and map views
API Testing — curl commands for testing Netlify functions locally
Development Tools — Server configuration for hot-reload and live testing
Why This Matters

This folder demonstrates a modern, AI-assisted development workflow where Claude was used not just for code, but for:

Strategic thinking about the project
Research and data organization
Problem-solving and debugging
Content and documentation

Rather than building in isolation, this project leveraged Claude as a collaborative development partner, showing how AI tools can enhance the entire development lifecycle.

Using Claude in Your Workflow

To replicate this approach:

Keep detailed notes on how Claude helped at each stage
Save configurations and settings that show integration
Document the thought process and problem-solving
Version control everything so the collaboration is visible

This transparency about AI tool usage is valuable for employers and shows sophistication in modern development practices.
